% compound_suspend.glp — FR-034 / SC-009: a guard whose operand is a COMPOUND
% containing a nested unbound reader MUST SUSPEND (not FAIL).
%
% Before the fix, the generic-guard path (_dereferenceWithTracking) returned a
% StructTerm operand as-is without recursing into its args, so a nested unbound
% reader was never collected: the guard passed the top-level suspend gate, then
% _termsEqual returned false on the unbound inner reader and the guard COMMITTED
% A FAIL — a non-monotone wrong commit. The fix recurses into compound args
% (reusing the same deref/collect machinery the dedicated GroundEqual opcode
% already applies), so the nested reader is collected and the guard SUSPENDS,
% reactivating once when the reader binds.
%
% The discriminating case is the term-equality guard `=?=` taken via the
% GENERIC path (a compound literal on the right-hand side, so the dedicated
% GroundEqual opcode — which never had the bug — is not used). NOTE: single
% clause per procedure — no fallback [] clause that would mask the bug by
% providing an alternative suspension path.

% (1) SUSPEND case: C is bound (head) to a compound carrying a nested unbound
% reader; `C? =?= pair(a, b)` must suspend, not commit a FAIL.
exported procedure eq_compound(_?, Constant).
eq_compound(C, yes) :- C? =?= pair(a, b) | true.

% (2) REACTIVATION case: a sibling goal binds the nested reader to the matching
% value; the suspended guard wakes exactly once and yields the ground verdict
% (the whole goal succeeds).
exported procedure run_eq_wake.
run_eq_wake :- eq_compound(pair(a, X?), _), waker_b(X).

exported procedure waker_b(_).
waker_b(b).

% (3) NEGATIVE control: a nested unbound WRITER is a definite FAIL (SRSW: no
% paired reader can supply the value), proving the fix does not over-suspend.
% Exercised by goal: eq_compound(pair(a, W), _).

% (4) ground/1 over the same compound also suspends on the nested reader (the
% already-correct path; kept as a companion sanity check).
exported procedure check_ground(_?).
check_ground(C) :- ground(C?) | done.

exported procedure done.
done.
